[
    {
        "content": "<p>rvolosatovs opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14743\">PR #14743</a> from <code>rvolosatovs:wasi-http-io-task-ownership</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The task driving an outbound request's connection was kept alive by three references: the transmission future, the response body and the request body. The request body reference is circular in the default <code>send_request</code> implementation, since the request body is owned by the hyper connection that the task itself drives. A guest could therefore leave connections running after the store was dropped, with no way for the embedder to reclaim them, e.g. by feeding an endless upstream response body into another outbound request.</p>\n<p>Drop the request and transmission future references and instead have the store hold a reference to the task until it finishes. Dropping the store now cancels every outbound connection not referenced by something the embedder holds, while a response body handed to the host unchanged keeps its connection alive for as long as the host reads it.</p>\n<p>As a consequence, the guest dropping all of its handles no longer cancels the task; it runs until it finishes or the store is dropped.</p>\n<p>Refs <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14633\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14633</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631709677,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1791996386
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>rvolosatovs requested <a href=\"https://github.com/alexcrichton\">alexcrichton</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14743\">PR #14743</a>.</p>",
