    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> adamrk submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14743#pullrequestreview-5522346964\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Much nicer than what I had before!</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631730020,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792001068
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> adamrk created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14743#discussion_r4274407113\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So I guess one difference here is that the guest can't cancel the io by dropping the response body anymore, right? (The drop just decrements the Arc ref count). Would it make sense to wrap this io in a type that cancels on drop?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 631730023,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1792001068
    },
